course: dictionary
lesson: 14886
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The words around them, the context, tell you which meaning to use. Reclaimed is a good example. «I reclaimed my lost bag from the lost property desk.» Here reclaimed means got back something that was yours.
explain: «The table was made from reclaimed wood.» Reclaimed wood is wood that was saved and used again instead of being thrown away. The word wood tells you this is not about getting something back.
explain: «The Dutch reclaimed land from the sea.» Here reclaimed means made usable again, for example by draining the water away. Ask yourself: what is being reclaimed? Land, not a person or a bag. Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Reclaim means to get back something that was yours.
fact: «Reclaimed» is the past form of «reclaim», so it describes something that was got back, or was saved and used again.
fact: «Reclaimed wood» and «reclaimed bricks» are old materials that were saved and used again instead of being thrown away.
fact: «Reclaimed land» is land made usable again, for example by draining the sea or cleaning polluted ground.
fact: «Reclaim your luggage» means collect the bags that belong to you at the airport.
exercise: «I reclaimed my lost bag from the lost property desk.» What does reclaimed mean here? | Bought a new bag | *Got back something that was mine | Hid it from my friends | Threw it away
exercise: «The shop sells chairs made from reclaimed wood.» What does reclaimed mean? | *Saved and used again instead of thrown away | Cut into tiny pieces | Painted in bright colours | Brand new and never used
exercise: «The Dutch reclaimed land from the sea.» What does reclaimed mean here? | Sold the sea to a company | Put a fence around the sea | *Made usable again, for example by draining the water | Covered the land in snow
test: Which meaning fits «reclaimed» in «The charity reclaimed the boy from a dangerous life on the streets»? | *Rescued from a bad way of life | Counted the children | Lost on the streets | Painted the school
test: «Mia's old bricks were reclaimed for her garden wall.» What does reclaimed mean? | Broken into dust | Bought from a shop | *Saved and used again instead of thrown away | Lost in the garden
exam: Which sentence uses reclaimed to mean made usable again? | «He reclaimed the lost dog from the park.» | «They reclaimed the old song from the radio.» | «She reclaimed her seat on the train.» | *«The engineers reclaimed the marsh by draining it.»
